258
00:17:15,493 --> 00:17:17,290
So he wasn't trying to wound us!

259
00:17:17,373 --> 00:17:19,070
He was dousing our bodies with gasoline!

260
00:17:19,153 --> 00:17:20,800
We're covered in this stuff!

261
00:17:22,733 --> 00:17:26,453
Looks like you finally caught
on, but it's too late now!

262
00:17:26,873 --> 00:17:28,873
Now all you need is a little jolt!

263
00:17:33,633 --> 00:17:34,753
Ah! Jotaro!

264
00:17:41,193 --> 00:17:43,853
Jotaro! Mr. Joestar! Stay back!

265
00:17:44,033 --> 00:17:45,690
We're soaking with gasoline, too!

266
00:17:45,773 --> 00:17:46,891
It's too dangerous!

267
00:17:52,573 --> 00:17:53,403
Chotaro!

268
00:17:54,813 --> 00:17:56,093
I win!

269
00:17:56,393 --> 00:17:59,113
Your valiant hero finally bit the dust!

270
00:18:06,893 --> 00:18:07,723
Is that so?

271
00:18:07,993 --> 00:18:11,453
And who exactly would
replace me, Chotaro Cujo?

272
00:18:18,433 --> 00:18:21,553
Let me guess, you thought
it'd be you, you roadhog.

273
00:18:23,113 --> 00:18:25,937
You burrowed into the
ground with star platinum,

274
00:18:26,113 --> 00:18:28,995
so the only thing that
burned up was your jacket!

275
00:18:29,633 --> 00:18:31,253
A little parting wisdom.

276
00:18:31,613 --> 00:18:35,993
What you said earlier
about paths was dead wrong.

277
00:18:36,473 --> 00:18:39,414
You see, in life, you have
to forge your own path.

278
00:18:39,693 --> 00:18:43,105
No one can do it for you, so
I'll offer you some guidance.

279
00:18:44,673 --> 00:18:47,853
Oh, but first you have to
go through a little pain

280
00:18:55,173 --> 00:18:56,633
A big crush.

281
00:18:56,793 --> 00:18:57,773
No, Jotaro.

282
00:19:01,453 --> 00:19:02,283
No!

283
00:19:03,393 --> 00:19:04,253
I love you.

284
00:19:09,493 --> 00:19:11,133
That is how it's done.

285
00:19:12,033 --> 00:19:14,033
See, you just paved your own path.

286
00:19:14,173 --> 00:19:16,114
Congrats on being a fast learner.

287
00:19:16,213 --> 00:19:17,573
Here ends the lesson.

288
00:19:24,813 --> 00:19:26,313
What an odd guy.

289
00:19:26,633 --> 00:19:30,833
His arms are the size of boulders
and yet everything else is so small.

290
00:19:31,333 --> 00:19:32,593
Talk about a bluff.

291
00:19:37,833 --> 00:19:38,663
Hello.

292
00:19:38,746 --> 00:19:39,576
Going somewhere?

293
00:19:42,053 --> 00:19:43,288
Please don't kill me!

294
00:19:43,453 --> 00:19:45,277
I'm just sinners for the money!

295
00:20:00,013 --> 00:20:01,793
Oh, would you look at that,

296
00:20:01,993 --> 00:20:06,070
I can't believe the stand was disguising
such a small car that entire time.

297
00:20:06,153 --> 00:20:10,977
Kinda reminds me of a fluffy little sheep
that just had all of its wool shorn off.

298
00:20:12,033 --> 00:20:14,293
What a pathetic hunk of junk!

299
00:20:15,093 --> 00:20:16,633
Ha ha ha ha ha!

300
00:20:27,033 --> 00:20:29,857
Well then, let's take his
car across the border.

301
00:20:30,013 --> 00:20:32,013
Only fair since he smashed ours.

302
00:20:32,313 --> 00:20:33,730
He's pretty beat up, though.

303
00:20:33,813 --> 00:20:35,754
I wonder if it'll last that long?

304
00:20:36,593 --> 00:20:37,553
Help! Help!

305
00:20:38,613 --> 00:20:41,650
You're on the next flight to Hong
Kong once we find an airport.

306
00:20:41,733 --> 00:20:42,970
Oh, I know what!

307
00:20:43,053 --> 00:20:43,973
Shut up!

308
00:20:44,233 --> 00:20:47,821
Don't you understand that you're
in the way, you little brat?

309
00:20:48,273 --> 00:20:50,713
We might not make it that far.

310
00:21:13,553 --> 00:21:18,453
My seven assassins have all
been defeated, and so easily!

311
00:21:19,613 --> 00:21:23,313
How could they be crushed
like that? The shame!

312
00:21:23,733 --> 00:21:26,053
I cannot bear to face Lordeo!

313
00:21:28,333 --> 00:21:29,433
Damn you!

314
00:21:29,613 --> 00:21:30,810
Curse you, Polnareff!

315
00:21:30,893 --> 00:21:32,053
Curse Kakyoin!

316
00:21:32,253 --> 00:21:34,724
Curse Jotaro and his wretched grandfather!

317
00:21:38,473 --> 00:21:42,653
I, Inyava, shall be your
next and final opponent!

318
00:21:43,133 --> 00:21:47,493
I will fight with my very own
stand, the stand of justice!

319
00:22:05,333 --> 00:22:08,010
All the old paintings on the tomb.

320
00:22:08,093 --> 00:22:10,050
They do the sand dance, don't you know?

321
00:22:10,133 --> 00:22:11,693
If they move too quick!

322
00:22:12,353 --> 00:22:14,750
They're falling down like a domino.

323
00:22:14,833 --> 00:22:17,370
All the birds are men by the Nile.

324
00:22:17,453 --> 00:22:21,050
They've got their money on
a bed called crocodiles.

325
00:22:21,133 --> 00:22:24,010
They snap their teeth on your cigarette.

326
00:22:24,093 --> 00:22:26,270
Falling tight to the hook I say.

327
00:22:33,153 --> 00:22:35,233
Walk like an Egyptian.

328
00:22:46,913 --> 00:22:50,010
The blonde waitresses take their trays.

329
00:22:50,093 --> 00:22:52,010
Spin around and they cross the floor.

330
00:22:52,093 --> 00:22:54,510
They've got the moves, oh-hey-oh.

331
00:22:54,593 --> 00:22:56,650
You drop your drink,
then they bring you more.

332
00:22:56,733 --> 00:22:59,290
All the school kids so sick of books.

333
00:22:59,373 --> 00:23:01,350
They're like the punk and the metal band.

334
00:23:01,433 --> 00:23:02,913
When the buzzer rings!

335
00:23:03,733 --> 00:23:05,610
They're walking like an Egyptian.

336
00:23:05,693 --> 00:23:08,250
All the kids in the marketplace say?

337
00:23:08,333 --> 00:23:09,210
Walk

338
00:23:09,293 --> 00:23:16,293
like

339
00:23:16,413 --> 00:23:17,243
an Egyptian.

340
00:23:20,073 --> 00:23:21,830
The fog looks thicker up ahead.

341
00:23:21,913 --> 00:23:23,670
He's dead with that look of fear.

342
00:23:23,753 --> 00:23:25,929
What is with the people in this town?

343
00:23:26,033 --> 00:23:27,621
This is no ordinary murder.

344
00:23:27,773 --> 00:23:29,750
The Joestar Party is on the third floor.

345
00:23:29,833 --> 00:23:32,009
Well, hello, I see you are traveling.

346
00:23:32,533 --> 00:23:34,493
Ah, salaam alaykum.
